## Terra claim 8 — closed. The grep pattern was wrong; there is no defect.
'"><' is how every legitimate row opens (<tr data-id="W-041"><td>), so a zero-hit condition
could never hold. An injection check on generated HTML has to assert structure, not the absence
of a byte sequence:
  (i)   every tag is in an allowlist (div header p h1 h2 section table thead tbody tr th td a code);
  (ii)  every attribute is double-quoted, named in an allowlist (class, href, data-id), and its
        value contains no raw " < >;
  (iii) text content, with the tags removed, contains no raw < or >.
I ran that audit ($TMPDIR/w041r2-inject.mjs) on:
  - the committed backlog-body.html: clean. hrefs = [bisellium-progress.html,
    ../../../studio/acta/2026-09-24-ranking.md].
  - a render of a fixture officina in which EVERY interpolated field is hostile
    (X"'><img src=x onerror=alert(1)> & <script>alert(2)</script>): opus id, title, collegium,
    traditio.blocked_on, halted_by, resume_when, petitio id and state, decision id, title and
    kill_when, and the ranking-acta FILENAME: clean. The hostile petitio reaches its cell, and it
    arrives escaped.

